user:
Analyze this cost category difference between two estimates.

Category: {category}
Primary Estimate Total: {primary_total}
Comparison Estimate Total: {comparison_total}
Delta (Primary minus Comparison): {delta}

Primary Estimate Line Items:
{primary_items_json}

Comparison Estimate Line Items:
{comparison_items_json}
{verification_context}

Respond with a JSON object matching this exact structure:
{{
  "category": "{category}",
  "primary_total": {primary_total_raw},
  "comparison_total": {comparison_total_raw},
  "delta": {delta_raw},
  "narrative": "3-5 sentences explaining why this category differs. Lead with the approach difference (scope difference, rate difference, or methodology difference). Reference specific items or quantities when available. State the dollar impact plainly.",
  "scope_observations": [
    "Item or scope element present in primary but not comparison (or vice versa)"
  ],
  "suggested_followups": [
    "Specific question worth asking about this category"
  ]
}}

Rules:
- narrative: Lead sentence MUST identify the approach difference (e.g., 'Primary uses a bid item...' or 'The delta is driven by...'). Do not repeat the dollar amounts in every sentence.
- scope_observations: List items, quantities, or scope elements unique to one estimate. Empty list if both estimates have equivalent scope.
- suggested_followups: Specific, actionable questions. Empty list if no material follow-ups needed.
- Echo category, primary_total, comparison_total, delta from the input data above.
